  "course_description": "This interdisciplinary course explores the history, politics, and cultures of transgender, intersex, and gender variant people in North America and beyond. It demonstrates that trans and intersex people have been central to the development of the contemporary analytics of sex, gender, and sexuality.",
  "course_notes": "This interdisciplinary course examines the histories, politics, and cultural formations of trans and gender-diverse lives across Asia and the Pacific. Through scholarship, media, and activism, students explore locally grounded categories¿including hijra, kathoey, kuaxingbie, X-gender, and zhongxing¿and consider how gender diversity intersects with race, class, migration, nationality, religion, and language. Using critical regionalist and decolonial approaches, the course challenges Western-centric frameworks and situates local experiences within global debates about gender, sexuality, and belonging.",
